From 42bb46368d34a9dfc4eaac01d3707d16895c2db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:35:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Shared verified-chain at A's final 554a251c (opt-in CLI/MCP
 additions); admission and metal bundles rebuilt

network/verified-chain.mjs is taken whole from A's immutable 554a251cbe14aa7ba8af4c160d9a8b9793e4071a (40f2b0a95): this
tree's copy was A's own base (c3a61fd1a e55f0359), so one source tree no longer carries a stale shared module. The
additions are opt-in per caller: pinnedClient/createVerifiedSnapshot `allowCall` (default off) and verifierRequest /
verifierClient (used by A's CLI custody and credit-vault readers). No Windows, network, relay or metal caller opts in.

test/verified-chain-optin-boundary.test.mjs pins that boundary: without allowCall a pinned client or default snapshot has
no raw `call` (refused by name, nothing sent); with it, eth_call is pinned to the block hash; verifierRequest refuses
everything but pinned state, headers by number and the head; no windows/, network/, relay/ or metal/ source uses them.

Rebuilt from this tree (scripts/build-host-admission.mjs, --check clean): windows/node/host-admission.bundle.mjs and
metal/guest/host-policy.bundle.mjs (the latter a Linux image input; no image is rebuilt). Left to A: cli/ and mcp/
changes of e32dd607b..554a251c and metal/guest/mcp-server.bundle.mjs (not part of this lineage).
